  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of archived Alaska Medicaid H.P. Acthar Gel (repository corticotropin / ACTH gel), injection 80 unit/mL. Effective date 2018-08-17 retained from metadata; PDF Effective 1/15/2019.",
    "Table 1 approval paths and shared contraindications encoded using indication when gates. Documentation and clinical facts are attestations; verification requires manual review.",
    "Second-level review required for ALL Table 2 grandfathered diagnoses for appropriateness and strength of clinical evidence. Encoded membership, contraindications, clinic notes, LMN documenting prior medications and at least one supporting peer-reviewed study with patient meeting inclusion criteria do not replace this review. Detailed clinical gates below remain notes only.",
    "Table 2 optic neuritis: adequate trial of two corticosteroids; ophthalmologist prescriber.",
    "Table 2 polymyositis/systemic dermatomyositis: adequate immunosuppressant and corticosteroid trials; may be used during acute exacerbation; dermatologist or rheumatologist prescriber.",
    "Table 2 proteinuria in nephrotic syndrome: induce diuresis/remission of proteinuria OR treat acute exacerbation; currently taking symptomatic therapy (diuretics, ACE inhibitor, ARB).",
    "Table 2 psoriatic arthritis: adequate trials of two corticosteroids; maintenance therapy (TNF blocker, DMARD, biologic); short-term adjunct for acute exacerbation; rheumatologist or dermatologist.",
    "Table 2 rheumatoid arthritis: adequate trials of two corticosteroids and two NSAIDs; maintenance therapy (TNF blocker, DMARD, biologic); short-term adjunct for acute exacerbation; rheumatologist.",
    "Table 2 SLE: adequate trials of two corticosteroids and one NSAID; maintenance therapy (immunosuppressant, biologic); short-term adjunct for acute exacerbation. Ankylosing spondylitis and symptomatic sarcoidosis require the shared Table 2 documentation and second-level review.",
    "Reauthorization (notes only): all initial criteria plus documented positive clinical response and clinic notes detailing response; deny if these are not met.",
    "Length of authorization (notes only): infantile spasms up to 4 weeks; acute MS exacerbation up to 21 days; Table 2 diagnoses up to 4 weeks.",
    "Quantity limit (notes only): 80 units/day (30 mL = 6 vials) per 30 days. max_units is null.",
    "Mechanism of action (notes only): unknown in infantile spasms; ACTH stimulates adrenal corticosteroid and weak androgen secretion and binds melanocortin receptors. Prolonged high doses cause adrenal hyperplasia/hypertrophy; cortisol feedback suppresses endogenous ACTH. Pharmacokinetics are not adequately characterized."
  ],
